number = 1898
title = "[Coherence] The three arbiter findings of 22.31.252 are marked resolved, but the arbiter crate does not compile on main and the replay case they cite is a known failure waiting on pending task 22.39.183"
revision = "3520b1428059af90261432778c008a9ce362a0b1"
verdict = "already-fixed"
evidence = "Commit fb88b2b94c684f1bcb6a24532a966af789447b0c repaired the historical codec imports at programs/crates/layerx-programs-arbiter/src/admission.rs:10 and programs/crates/layerx-programs-arbiter/src/activity_codec.rs:1, and commit dd3a58600392bfe151306e605f4dddc12d6fce97 repaired record-header transport at programs/crates/layerx-programs-arbiter/tests/proof_arbiter_crate.rs:1214 and authenticated raw-leaf decoding at programs/crates/layerx-programs-arbiter/src/market.rs:31, retaining authenticated execution at programs/crates/layerx-programs-arbiter/tests/proof_arbiter_crate.rs:944, the million-unit CPU cap at programs/crates/layerx-programs-arbiter/tests/proof_arbiter_crate.rs:957 and every adjacent-pair replay assertion at programs/crates/layerx-programs-arbiter/tests/proof_arbiter_crate.rs:1541, with both prerequisite tasks now done at spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:187669 and spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:187702, so the resolved dispositions at spec/layerx-merge/dispositions/d22-18.kvx:46 no longer conceal the cited defects."
close_comment = "The arbiter now uses the historical activity codec and verifies authenticated replay leaves with their record headers, preserving the CPU limit and adjacent-pair replay checks. Both repairs have landed, so the three findings can remain resolved."
